  "question": {
    "text": "A force $\\left(3 x^2+2 x-5\\right) \\mathrm{N}$ displaces a body from $x=2 \\mathrm{~m}$ to $x=4 \\mathrm{~m}$. Work done by this force is ________ $J$.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "58",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & W=\\int_{x_1}^{x_2} F d x \\\\ & W=\\int_2^4\\left(3 x^2+2 x-5\\right) d x \\\\ & W=\\left[x^3+x^2-5 x\\right]_2^4 \\\\ & W=[60-2] J=58 J\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
